Sending keys: ['cat > /root/patches/README.md << \'EOF\'\n# Apache Druid 0.20.0 Security Patch - CVE-2020-1938\n\n## Vulnerability Description\n\nApache Druid versions up to 0.20.0 contain a vulnerability in the JavaScript filter implementation that allows authenticated attackers to execute arbitrary code on the server. The vulnerability exists in the way Jackson deserializes filter specifications when `FAIL_ON_UNKNOWN_PROPERTIES` is set to false.\n\nAttackers can bypass JavaScript security restrictions by including an empty string key (`""`) in the JSON payload with a malicious configuration object:\n\n```json\n{\n  "type": "javascript",\n  "function": "function(){java.lang.Runtime.getRuntime().exec(\'malicious_command\');}",\n  "": {\n    "enabled": true\n  }\n}\n```\n\n## Fix Description\n\nThis patch adds validation to the `JavaScriptDimFilter` class to:\n\n1. **Block Dangerous Java API Calls**: The `validateConfiguration()` method checks if the JavaScript function contains calls to dangerous Java APIs that could be used for code execution:\n   - `java.lang.Runtime`\n   - `java.lang.ProcessBuilder`\n   - `java.io.File`\n\n2. **Early Validation**: The validation is performed in the constructor, ensuring that malicious payloads are rejected immediately upon deserialization.\n\n## Files Modified\n\n- `processing/src/main/java/org/apache/druid/query/filter/JavaScriptDimFilter.java`\n  - Added `validateConfiguration()` method\n  - Added validation call in the `@JsonCreator` constructor\n\n## Patch Files\n\n- `0001-fix-javascript-filter-empty-key-vulnerability.patch` - Main security fix\n\n## How to Apply\n\n1. Navigate to the Druid source directory:\n   ```bash\n   cd /root/druid\n   ```\n\n2. Apply the patch:\n   ```bash\n   git apply /root/patches/0001-fix-javascript-filter-empty-key-vulnerability.patch\n   ```\n\n3. Rebuild the affected modules:\n   ```bash\n   mvn clean package -DskipTests -Dcheckstyle.skip=true -Dpmd.skip=true \\\n     -Dforbiddenapis.skip=true -Dspotbugs.skip=true -Danimal.sniffer.skip=true \\\n     -Denforcer.skip=true -Djacoco.skip=true -Ddependency-check.skip=true \\\n     -pl \'!web-console\' -pl indexing-service -am\n   ```\n\n4. Deploy the patched JAR files:\n   - `druid-processing-0.20.0.jar` to `/opt/druid/lib/`\n   - `druid-indexing-service-0.20.0.jar` to `/opt/druid/lib/`\n\n## Verification\n\nAfter applying the patch, the following behavior should be observed:\n\n1. **Legitimate JavaScript filters** (without dangerous API calls) continue to work normally\n2. **Malicious payloads** containing Java API calls are rejected with an `IllegalArgumentException`\n3. **Empty key payloads** are safely ignored by Jackson and don\'t bypass security checks\n\n## Testing\n\nThe fix can be tested by attempting to create a JavaScript filter with a dangerous API call:\n\n```json\nPOST /druid/indexer/v1/sampler HTTP/1.1\nContent-Type: application/json\n\n{\n  "type": "index",\n  "spec": {\n    "dataSchema": {\n      "transformSpec": {\n        "filter": {\n          "type": "javascript",\n          "function": "function(){java.lang.Runtime.getRuntime().exec(\'id\');}"\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\nExpected result: The request should be rejected with an error message about dangerous Java API calls.\n\nEOF\ncat /root/patches/README.md\n'] min_timeout_sec: 0.5 max_timeout_sec: 180.0
