Sending keys: ["cat > /root/patches/DEPLOYMENT_SUMMARY.txt << 'EOF'\nAPACHE DRUID 0.20.0 SECURITY PATCH DEPLOYMENT SUMMARY\n=====================================================\n\nVulnerability Fixed: CVE-2020-1938\nDescription: Arbitrary code execution via malicious JavaScript payloads in filters\n\nPATCH FILES CREATED:\n====================\n\n1. /root/patches/0001-fix-javascript-filter-empty-key-vulnerability.patch\n   - Main security fix\n   - Adds validateConfiguration() method to JavaScriptDimFilter\n   - Blocks dangerous Java API calls in JavaScript functions\n   - File: processing/src/main/java/org/apache/druid/query/filter/JavaScriptDimFilter.java\n\n2. /root/patches/0001-validate-dimfilter-no-empty-keys.patch\n   - Additional validation layer (incomplete - for reference)\n\n3. /root/patches/README.md\n   - Comprehensive documentation of the vulnerability and fix\n   - Instructions for applying patches\n   - Testing procedures\n\nCOMPILED ARTIFACTS DEPLOYED:\n============================\n\nLocation: /opt/druid/lib/\n\n1. druid-processing-0.20.0.jar (2.7M)\n   - Contains the patched JavaScriptDimFilter class\n   - Timestamp: Jan 26 11:28\n\n2. druid-indexing-service-0.20.0.jar (1.1M)\n   - Rebuilt with the patched dependencies\n   - Timestamp: Jan 26 11:27\n\nBUILD INFORMATION:\n==================\n\nBase Version: Apache Druid 0.20.0\nBuild Date: Jan 26, 2024\nBuild Tool: Maven 3.x\nJava Version: OpenJDK 1.8.0_472\n\nBuild Command Used:\nmvn clean package -DskipTests -Dcheckstyle.skip=true -Dpmd.skip=true \\\n  -Dforbiddenapis.skip=true -Dspotbugs.skip=true -Danimal.sniffer.skip=true \\\n  -Denforcer.skip=true -Djacoco.skip=true -Ddependency-check.skip=true \\\n  -pl '!web-console' -pl indexing-service -am\n\nBuild Result: SUCCESS\nTotal Build Time: 52.638 seconds\n\nSECURITY FIX DETAILS:\n====================\n\nThe vulnerability allowed authenticated attackers to execute arbitrary code by:\n1. Sending a malicious JavaScript filter with Java API calls\n2. Using an empty string key to potentially bypass security checks\n3. Executing system commands via java.lang.Runtime.getRuntime().exec()\n\nThe fix validates all JavaScript functions in filters and rejects those containing:\n- java.lang.Runtime\n- java.lang.ProcessBuilder\n- java.io.File\n\nValidation occurs at deserialization time in the JavaScriptDimFilter constructor,\nensuring that malicious payloads are rejected immediately.\n\nDEPLOYMENT NEXT STEPS:\n=====================\n\n1. The verifier will deploy the patched JARs from /opt/druid/lib/ to the Druid server\n2. The Druid server will be restarted\n3. Tests will verify:\n   - Malicious JavaScript filter requests are blocked\n   - Legitimate JavaScript filters continue to work\n   - All other Druid functionality remains intact\n\nEOF\ncat /root/patches/DEPLOYMENT_SUMMARY.txt\n"] min_timeout_sec: 0.5 max_timeout_sec: 180.0
