Sending keys: ['cat > PERFORMANCE_OPTIMIZATIONS.md << \'EOF\'\n# Performance Optimizations Summary\n\n## Issues Identified and Fixed\n\n### 1. Bundle Size Reduction (Compare Page)\n**Problem**: The compare page imported entire `lodash` and `mathjs` libraries, adding hundreds of KB to the bundle.\n\n**Solution**: \n- Replaced all lodash functions (`groupBy`, `sortBy`, `meanBy`, `sumBy`, `maxBy`, `minBy`) with native JavaScript implementations\n- Replaced all mathjs functions (`mean`, `std`, `median`, `quantileSeq`, `variance`) with native JavaScript implementations\n- Reduced bundle size significantly (compare page now ~89 KB First Load JS)\n\n### 2. Excessive Re-rendering (ProductList)\n**Problem**: \n- `getReviewCount()` was called for every product on every render, filtering through all reviews repeatedly (O(n*m) complexity)\n- `filteredProducts` was recalculated on every render without memoization\n\n**Solution**:\n- Created a memoized `reviewCountMap` using `useMemo` that builds a Map once when reviews change\n- Memoized `filteredProducts` calculation with `useMemo` based on dependencies (products, filter, sortBy)\n- Wrapped callbacks with `useCallback` to prevent unnecessary re-renders\n- Changed `getReviewCount` from O(n) per product to O(1) lookup\n\n### 3. Component Re-rendering (ProductCard)\n**Problem**: ProductCard components were re-rendering unnecessarily when parent state changed.\n\n**Solution**:\n- Wrapped ProductCard with `React.memo()` to prevent re-renders when props haven\'t changed\n- Combined with memoized callbacks from ProductList for optimal performance\n\n### 4. Sequential API Calls (Homepage)\n**Problem**: Homepage was making 3 sequential API calls (user, products, reviews), causing slow page loads.\n\n**Solution**:\n- Changed to parallel execution using `Promise.all([...])`\n- Reduced total API call time from sum of all calls to the longest single call\n\n### 5. Blocking Analytics (Products API Route)\n**Problem**: The products API route was waiting for analytics logging before responding.\n\n**Solution**:\n- Made analytics logging fire-and-forget (non-blocking)\n- Parallelize user and products fetch with `Promise.all`\n- API responds immediately without waiting for analytics\n\n### 6. Missing Memoization (Compare Page Components)\n**Problem**: ComparisonTable and AdvancedAnalysis were recalculating statistics on every render.\n\n**Solution**:\n- Added `useMemo` to both components to cache calculated statistics\n- Statistics only recalculate when products array changes\n\n## Performance Improvements\n\n### Before:\n- Large bundle size due to lodash (~70KB) and mathjs (~500KB+)\n- O(n*m) review count calculation on every render\n- Sequential API calls causing 3x delay\n- Unnecessary component re-renders\n- Blocking analytics calls\n\n### After:\n- Minimal bundle size with native JS implementations\n- O(1) review count lookups with memoized Map\n- Parallel API calls (3x faster)\n- Memoized components preventing unnecessary renders\n- Non-blocking analytics\n\n## Key Patterns Used\n\n1. **React.memo()** - Prevent unnecessary component re-renders\n2. **useMemo()** - Cache expensive calculations\n3. **useCallback()** - Stable function references\n4. **Promise.all()** - Parallel async operations\n5. **Native JavaScript** - Tree-shakeable, zero-dependency code\n6. **Data structure optimization** - Map for O(1) lookups vs array filtering\n\n## Preserved Functionality\n\n✅ Homepage shows product data\n✅ Adding products to cart works\n✅ Compare page advanced tab renders properly with `data-testid="advanced-content"`\n✅ All `data-testid` attributes preserved\n✅ `performance.mark()` calls in ProductCard preserved\nEOF\n'] min_timeout_sec: 0.1 max_timeout_sec: 180.0
