Sending keys: ['cat > /tmp/VULNERABILITY_FIX_SUMMARY.md << \'EOF\'\n# Erlang/OTP SSH Unauthenticated Remote Command Execution Vulnerability Fix\n\n## Vulnerability Description\n\nA critical vulnerability was discovered in the Erlang/OTP SSH server that allows attackers to execute arbitrary system commands remotely WITHOUT authentication.\n\n### Root Cause\n\nThe vulnerability exists in `lib/ssh/src/ssh_connection_handler.erl`. The SSH connection handler processes SSH connection protocol messages (wrapped as `conn_msg` events) in ANY state of the connection state machine, including states BEFORE user authentication is complete.\n\n### Attack Vector\n\nAn attacker can:\n1. Initiate an SSH connection to the server\n2. Before completing authentication, send SSH protocol messages such as:\n   - `SSH_MSG_CHANNEL_REQUEST` with type "exec" to execute commands\n   - `SSH_MSG_CHANNEL_REQUEST` with type "shell" to open a shell\n   - `SSH_MSG_CHANNEL_REQUEST` with type "subsystem" to start subsystems\n3. These messages are processed by `ssh_connection:handle_msg()` which calls `handle_cli_msg()`\n4. The `handle_cli_msg()` function starts a CLI process and executes the requested command\n5. No authentication check is performed before command execution\n\n### Affected Code Path\n\n1. SSH messages are decoded in `handle_event()` around line 1187\n2. `SSH_MSG_CHANNEL_REQUEST` messages are wrapped as `{conn_msg, Msg}`\n3. The `handle_event(internal, {conn_msg,Msg}, StateName, ...)` clause at line 771 processes these messages\n4. This handler calls `ssh_connection:handle_msg()` regardless of the `StateName`\n5. For "exec" requests, this eventually calls `handle_cli_msg()` in `ssh_connection.erl`\n6. Commands are executed without verifying that authentication has completed\n\n## Fix Implementation\n\n### Location\nFile: `lib/ssh/src/ssh_connection_handler.erl`\nLines: 760-769 (new authentication check clause)\n\n### Fix Description\n\nAdded a new `handle_event` clause that intercepts `conn_msg` events when the connection is NOT in an authenticated state:\n\n```erlang\n%% Reject connection messages before authentication is complete\n%% This clause catches conn_msg in non-connected states (except during renegotiation)\nhandle_event(internal, {conn_msg,_Msg}, StateName, D)\n  when StateName =/= {connected,client}, StateName =/= {connected,server},\n       StateName =/= {kexinit,client,renegotiate}, StateName =/= {kexinit,server,renegotiate},\n       StateName =/= {ext_info,client,renegotiate}, StateName =/= {ext_info,server,renegotiate} ->\n    %% Connection messages should only be processed after successful authentication\n    Disconnect = #ssh_msg_disconnect{code = ?SSH_DISCONNECT_PROTOCOL_ERROR,\n                                      description = "Connection message received before authentication"},\n    {Repls, D1} = send_replies([{connection_reply, Disconnect}], D),\n    {stop_and_reply, {shutdown, "Protocol error"}, Repls, D1};\n```\n\n### How the Fix Works\n\n1. **Pattern Matching**: The new clause matches `conn_msg` events before the original handler\n2. **State Validation**: Uses guard clauses to check if the state is NOT one of:\n   - `{connected,client}` - authenticated client\n   - `{connected,server}` - authenticated server\n   - `{kexinit,client,renegotiate}` - client renegotiating keys\n   - `{kexinit,server,renegotiate}` - server renegotiating keys  \n   - `{ext_info,client,renegotiate}` - client in ext_info during renegotiation\n   - `{ext_info,server,renegotiate}` - server in ext_info during renegotiation\n3. **Rejection**: If in an unauthenticated state, sends `SSH_DISCONNECT_PROTOCOL_ERROR` and closes the connection\n4. **Fallthrough**: If authenticated or renegotiating, the message falls through to the original handler (line 771)\n\n### Security Impact\n\n- **Before Fix**: Attackers could execute arbitrary commands without authentication\n- **After Fix**: Connection messages (exec, shell, subsystem) are ONLY processed after successful authentication\n- **Normal Operation**: Legitimate authenticated sessions continue to work normally\n- **Renegotiation**: Key renegotiation during active sessions continues to work correctly\n\n## Verification\n\nThe fix ensures that:\n1. Unauthenticated SSH_MSG_CHANNEL_REQUEST messages are rejected\n2. The server responds with SSH_DISCONNECT_PROTOCOL_ERROR\n3. The connection is terminated before any command execution\n4. Authenticated sessions can still execute commands normally\n5. SSH key renegotiation continues to function properly\n\nEOF\ncat /tmp/VULNERABILITY_FIX_SUMMARY.md\n'] min_timeout_sec: 0.5 max_timeout_sec: 180.0
