Sending keys: ["cat > analysis_summary.txt << 'EOF'\nMARKET CLEARING ANALYSIS SUMMARY\n================================\n\nOBJECTIVE:\nAnalyze the impact of increasing the thermal capacity of transmission line 64-1501\nby 20% on the day-ahead market clearing results.\n\nMETHODOLOGY:\n- DC-OPF with reserve co-optimization\n- 2,869 buses, 510 generators, 4,582 transmission lines\n- Reserve requirement: 5,923.5 MW\n- Thermal capacity limits enforced on all transmission lines\n- Spinning reserve with standard capacity coupling constraints\n\nKEY FINDINGS:\n\n1. BASE CASE (Original network):\n   - Total system cost: $2,546,267.27 per hour\n   - Binding transmission lines: 29 (at or near thermal limits)\n   - Line 64-1501 capacity: 312.00 MW\n   - Reserve clearing price: $5.00/MWh\n\n2. COUNTERFACTUAL CASE (Line 64-1501 capacity +20%):\n   - Total system cost: $2,546,126.85 per hour\n   - Binding transmission lines: 28 (one less than base case)\n   - Line 64-1501 capacity: 374.40 MW (20% increase)\n   - Reserve clearing price: $5.00/MWh\n\n3. IMPACT ANALYSIS:\n   - Cost reduction: $140.42 per hour\n   - Annual savings (estimated): $1,229,484.80\n   - Congestion relief: YES (binding lines reduced from 29 to 28)\n   - Line 64-1501 status: No longer binding in counterfactual\n\n4. LOCATIONAL MARGINAL PRICES (LMPs):\n   - Most buses show stable LMPs between scenarios\n   - Top 3 buses with largest LMP drops identified\n   - System-wide price changes reflect reduced congestion\n\nCONCLUSION:\nRelaxing the thermal capacity constraint on line 64-1501 by 20% reduces the\ntotal system cost by $140.42/hour and relieves one binding transmission constraint.\nThis suggests that line 64-1501 was indeed a significant source of congestion in\nthe base case, contributing to higher market clearing prices.\n\nRECOMMENATIONS:\n- Consider infrastructure investment to increase line 64-1501 capacity\n- Monitor line 64-1501 loading in real-time operations\n- Evaluate cost-benefit of capacity upgrade ($1.23M annual savings potential)\n\nEOF\ncat analysis_summary.txt\n"] min_timeout_sec: 0.5 max_timeout_sec: 180.0
